  "notes": "Yamamoto-first discovery pass under the current durable repository authority. docs/PRIORITIES.md, docs/EDITORIAL.md, docs/DOMAINS.md, and radar/inbox/README.md were read before research or grading. Fresh Yamamoto checks did not produce a future verified appearance not already represented in canonical/curated/processed intake, so no duplicate Yamamoto record was created. The broader US-corridor pass found Public Works' PUBLIC RECORD at the revitalized Delacorte Theater. Stage 1 admits this specific production because the live event itself creates the artifact: more than 100 New Yorkers, musicians, dancers, a DJ, and a vocalist assemble a live album in real time for the North American premiere, with the resulting album designated for preservation by the New York Public Library for the Performing Arts. The billed music contributors include Louis Cato, Arturo O’Farrill, Arun Ramamurthy, and Mireya Ramos, giving the civic recording project a concrete cross-cultural live-music reason beyond venue prestige or famous names. Stage 2 assigns A. The current rubric expects A to remain the broad base, and this candidate does not add pressure to the scarcity tiers. The five-performance run and lack of a one-night-only musical lineup make attend-if-convenient the durable recommendation rather than actively reorganizing plans. No musical_axes tag is assigned because the current fixed filter set does not cleanly describe the whole production; tagging the entire event Latin solely because some billed musicians fit that axis would overstate one part of a deliberately plural project.",
