      "factual_description": "The Public Theater presents the North American premiere of Public Works' PUBLIC RECORD at the revitalized Delacorte Theater in Central Park from September 4 through September 8, 2026, with one performance at 20:00 each night. Based on a concept by Dan Canham and Emily Lim and written by Lisa Sanaye Dring, the production brings more than 100 New Yorkers together with professional musicians, dancers, a DJ, and a vocalist to create a live album onstage in real time. Michael Thurber provides original orchestrations and music supervision. The Public Theater bills Louis Cato, Arturo O’Farrill, Arun Ramamurthy, and Mireya Ramos among the musicians, Papi Juice as DJ, and Maya Margarita as vocalist. The resulting album is to be preserved by the New York Public Library for the Performing Arts. The performances are free, with day-of access distributed through official Public Theater channels including Central Park distribution, an in-person lottery, the TodayTix digital lottery, and a Central Park standby line.",
