          "why_it_matters": "The record is not documentation of the show; making the record is the show. More than 100 New Yorkers share the Delacorte with musicians including Louis Cato, Arturo O’Farrill, Arun Ramamurthy, and Mireya Ramos to build a live album in real time, and the finished artifact is intended for permanent preservation at the New York Public Library for the Performing Arts. That makes this a rare civic-music proposition: the city is being asked to hear itself while the archive is being created.",
